<title>POLAND: Wedel plans 1.2 zloty 1996 payout.</title>
<headline>Wedel plans 1.2 zloty 1996 payout.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The management of Polish confectioner Zaklady Przemyslu Cukierniczego E.Wedel SA will propose to shareholders a 1996 payout of 1.2 zlotys per share, the firm said in a Wednesday statement.</p>
<p>The management said it would propose that seven million zlotys from last year's 38.4 million net profit be allocated as dividends and the remaining 31.4 million zlotys be invested in further development of the firm.</p>
<p>It said the dividend on Wedel's fourth share issue, of 145,713 shares, would amount to 0.2 zlotys per share.</p>
<p>The planned record date is June 16 and the payment date is July 14, 1997, Wedel said.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
